   LET X = 9347
                   LET MAX_DIGIT = 0
                   WHILE X > 0
                       LET DIGIT = X % 10
                       IF DIGIT > MAX_DIGIT
                           LET MAX_DIGIT = DIGIT
                       LET X = X / 10
                   WEND
                   PRINT MAX_DIGIT

LET X = 9347
The interpreter assigns the value 9347 to the variable X. This is the number whose digits we want to analyze.

LET MAX_DIGIT = 0
The interpreter assigns 0 to the variable MAX_DIGIT. This will store the largest digit found as the code processes each digit of X.

WHILE X > 0
The interpreter starts a WHILE loop that runs as long as X is greater than 0. The loop will continue until all the digits of X have been processed.

LET DIGIT = X % 10
Inside the loop, the interpreter calculates X % 10 to extract the last digit of X. This result is stored in the variable DIGIT. For example, when X = 9347, X % 10 gives the last digit 7.

IF DIGIT > MAX_DIGIT THEN LET MAX_DIGIT = DIGIT
The interpreter checks if the current digit (DIGIT) is greater than MAX_DIGIT. If it is, it updates MAX_DIGIT with the value of DIGIT.

LET X = X / 10
The interpreter removes the last digit from X by performing integer division (X / 10). This effectively shifts the digits of X to the right. For example, 9347 / 10 results in 934 (the fractional part is discarded).

WEND
The interpreter goes back to the beginning of the WHILE loop and repeats steps 4 through 6 until X becomes 0.

Detailed Iteration:
First iteration (X = 9347):

DIGIT = 9347 % 10 = 7
MAX_DIGIT = 0, so MAX_DIGIT = 7 (since 7 > 0).
X = 9347 / 10 = 934.
Second iteration (X = 934):

DIGIT = 934 % 10 = 4
MAX_DIGIT = 7, so no change to MAX_DIGIT.
X = 934 / 10 = 93.
Third iteration (X = 93):

DIGIT = 93 % 10 = 3
MAX_DIGIT = 7, so no change to MAX_DIGIT.
X = 93 / 10 = 9.
Fourth iteration (X = 9):

DIGIT = 9 % 10 = 9
MAX_DIGIT = 7, so MAX_DIGIT = 9 (since 9 > 7).
X = 9 / 10 = 0.
WEND
The loop ends because X is now 0.

PRINT MAX_DIGIT
Finally, the interpreter prints the value of MAX_DIGIT, which is 9, since it is the largest digit found during the iterations.
